==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Bittersweet Mekako''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Minty Love Mekako''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is overall a long-ranged backliner with decent damage, high cooldown and a 50% chance to freeze her target traits, but lacks defensive abilities. As with the [[Justice Strikes Back! Dark Heroes (Gacha Event)|Dark Heroes]] Uber Set, each form takes on a different niche that players can switch to depending on their threat assessment. Unfortunately, since the freeze isn't guaranteed, you'll still have to rely on other sources of defense.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Sweet Love Mekako is one of the few anti-Traitless units, which puts her to great use as she doesn't have to wander into the line of fire, a fact prevalent in fights involving [[R.Ost]], featured in [[Hungry Forest]], [[Procrastinator Parade]], [[Birdwatching]], and many more. She also sees use in certain Crazed/Manic/Event stages like [[Vulcanizer (Deadly)|Vulcanizer]] ([[Manic Eraser Cat (Enemy)|Manic Eraser]]), but will need protection against enemy waves from attackers like [[Kory]] and [[Manic Macho Legs (Enemy)|Manic Macho Legs]], with no proper response against the likes of [[THE SLOTH]], [[Master A.]] [[Mr. Mole]], [[Henry]], [[Croakley]] and [[Kappy Jr.]] This often limits her use to a small selection of threats, and given how hard they can push with their abilities, she finds somewhat limited use.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Bittersweet Mekako, despite having much longer range, still gets outclassed by [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]], as the vast majority of Dark enemies are nasty melee pushers under 200 range. Bomber's 240 is more than enough to consistently deny many of these enemies, and while Bittersweet Mekako can hit [[Le'noir]]/[[Dark Lazer (Enemy)|Dark Lazer]], Le'noir is easy to stall while Dark Lazer is mostly an event enemy that is rarely fought. To top it off, her freeze effect does not always trigger, and while she does enough damage to ward off black pushers, she isn't doing much to kill them off. You're better off merely using attackers to nuke these enemies instead.

==='''True Form'''===
Minty Love Mekako, despite her newfound Relic target and curse immunity, is not the best at controlling such enemies, even if she can outrange them. Unlike your more reliable usual counters, Mekako's non-guaranteed freeze activation and the general aggression of nasty relics often mean if she fails to freeze them, she may not get another chance to attack. These attributes often cause her to fall behind the likes of [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapsticks]], [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Uril]] or even [[Medusa Cat (Rare Cat)|Naga]] as a proper response. As such, the extreme True Form cost cannot be justified, and you should save your Epic Seeds/Elder Fruit for things like Slapsticks, [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Amaterasu]] or even [[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Saki]] if you own them.

